<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adityasena</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">7th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adityasena was a king of the Later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gupta-empire">Gupta dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magadha">Magadha</a> in the second half of the 7th century. After the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harsha">Harsha</a> he restored his family's power in Magadha, took the title of maharajadhiraja and is said to have performed the horse sacrifice. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aphsad-inscription">Aphsad inscription</a> traces the dynasty from its founder, and his line kept ties with the Maukharis and with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>.</p></div>
